## Golden rules (always)

1. **Never push to `<PROD_BRANCH>` or production without the project owner's current-turn approval.**
2. Always start on `<BASE_BRANCH>`, freshly fetched. Run `<BUILD_COMMAND>` before commit.
3. Don't refactor outside the task. Preserve existing behaviour unless asked.
4. For data changes: trace UI → API → data → permissions → tests before touching.
5. <SENSITIVE_DATA_RULE — e.g. "Customer data is regulated; read `.claude/rules/security-privacy.md` before touching auth, exports or deletion.">
6. Don't read every doc. Use the routing map below.
7. **Before editing any file, read the `.claude/rules/*.md` whose `paths:` match it**, and list the
   rule files read in your final summary. (Path-scoped rules load when you read a matching file;
   the optional rule-surfacing hook covers files written blind.)
8. **Multi-agent handoffs are bidirectional and structured.** Orchestrator → specialist uses the
   outbound `handoff:` block in `docs/ai-context/HANDOFF_SCHEMA.md`; specialists validate it, refuse
   if vague, and end every response with the inbound `return:` block. **No evidence, no claim.**
9. **Corrections harden into rules.** If the owner corrected a *recurring* pattern this turn, end
   the turn by drafting a one-line patch to the right `.claude/rules/<file>.md` and ask for approval.
   Never say "I'll remember" — memory is machine-local and invisible to every other agent.
10. **Deferred work must be written, not spoken.** Any "later" / follow-up / known gap named in a
    summary is appended to `docs/<AREA>_BACKLOG.md` (what / why / effort / revisit-when) before the
    turn ends.
11. **Every production push freshens the docs — same turn, no exceptions.** `<CHANGELOG_PATH>`
    (the anchor), the affected orientation map(s), the affected rules, and `PROJECT.md` §3 if the
    production state changed. (Hook-enforced if `doc-freshness-gate` is installed.)
12. **One name per concept.** `docs/ai-context/GLOSSARY.md` is a rule file; adding a new name for
    an existing concept is a defect.
13. <OWNER_COMMUNICATION_RULE — optional; e.g. "Owner-facing messages use plain language; translate every technical term once." See `LEARNINGS.md` §E.>

## Mandatory workflow (every non-trivial task)

1. Restate the task. Identify affected roles.
2. Read `docs/ai-context/PROJECT.md` (current truth — especially §3, what is live where) and
   `docs/ai-context/INDEX.md`. Skim `docs/ai-context/LEARNINGS.md` §D before the first edit.
3. Read only the minimum docs flagged for the task (50–150 lines each).
4. For each file you plan to edit, read the matching `.claude/rules/*.md`.
5. Medium/complex tasks → `<PROJECT_SLUG>-orchestrator`. Handoffs use the schema (rule 8).
6. Inspect code before proposing changes. Smallest safe change.
7. Run the relevant checks. Verification follows the proof ladder in
   `.claude/skills/<PROJECT_SLUG>-engineering/SKILL.md` (a green build is evidence, not proof).
8. **Definition of done:** changed files, checks run with results, risks, follow-ups (written to a
   backlog), and the list of rule files read.

